  "caption": "Quinn's old warm-up: one side stretch, held for a heroic four seconds. The first sprint felt like the legs were still in bed.\n\nA good warm-up raises body temperature, wakes up the nervous system and rehearses the moves you're about to do. Long static stretches right before exercise can briefly sap strength and power, so save them for afterwards.\n\nA simple recipe: 2–4 minutes of easy cardio that gets brisker, 3–4 minutes of moving stretches like leg swings and arm circles, then rehearse the session with an empty bar, strides or direction changes. Go a bit longer on cold mornings.\n\nPain during the warm-up that sticks around into your session is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
